[Event "Vienna: 2...Nf6 3.f4"]

{The Vienna develops the queen's knight first so that f2-f4 can come with more support. It is aggressive but sound.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... e5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls d4 and f4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
2. Nc3 {[%csl Gd5] The Vienna: supports e4 and keeps the f-pawn free for f4.}
2... Nf6 {Develops and hits e4. The knight on f6 controls d5 and eyes the pawn on e4.}
3. f4 {[%cal Gf4e5] The Vienna Gambit: White attacks e5 at once. Supports the centre: the pawn on f4 controls g5 and eyes the pawn on e5. That pawn is currently undefended.}
3... d5 {The principled reply: counter in the centre. The pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
 (3... exf4 {Grabs the pawn but cedes the centre. Takes the pawn on f4, and it cannot be taken back at once.}
4. e5 {[%cal Ge5f6] Kicks the knight. Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls d6 and eyes the knight on f6.}
4... Ng8 {Back home; Black accepts a loss of time to keep the pawn.}
5. Nf3 {Develops and stops ...Qh4+. The knight on f3 controls d4 and supports the pawn on e5.}
5... d6 {Strikes at e5. Supports the centre: the pawn on d6 controls c5 and eyes the pawn on e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8.}
6. d4 {[%csl Ge5,Gd4] Builds a big centre and opens the c1-bishop to take f4.}
)
4. fxe5 {Gains space and drives the knight once ...Nxe4.}
4... Nxe4 {The knight jumps to a central outpost. Takes the pawn on e4; White will want to recapture.}
5. Nf3 {Develops and covers d4/h4. The knight on f3 controls d4 and supports the pawn on e5.}
5... Be7 {Develops calmly. The bishop on e7 controls f6 and d6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
 (5... Nc6 {Develops and eyes e5. The knight on c6 controls d4 and eyes the pawn on e5.}
6. Bb5 {[%cal Gb5c6] Pins and pressures the defender of e5. Develops the bishop to b5, where it controls c4 and eyes the knight on c6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
)
6. d4 {[%csl Ge5,Gd4] Strong centre. White will play Bd3 and O-O. The pawn on d4 controls c5 and supports the pawn on e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7. Bd3 {[%cal Gd3e4] Challenges the e4 knight. Develops the bishop to d3, where it eyes the knight on e4. That clears the way to castle kingside.} *

[Event "Vienna: 2...Nc6 & 2...Bc5"]

{The Vienna can also be played positionally with Bc4, d3 and f4.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... e5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls d4 and f4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
2. Nc3 {The Vienna. Develops the knight to c3, where it controls d5 and supports the pawn on e4.}
2... Nc6 {Symmetrical development. The knight on c6 controls d4 and supports the pawn on e5.}
 (2... Bc5 {Active bishop. Develops the bishop to c5, where it controls d4.}
3. Nf3 {Develops and attacks e5. The knight on f3 controls d4 and eyes the pawn on e5. That pawn is currently undefended.}
3... d6 {Supports e5. Supports the centre: the pawn on d6 supports the bishop on c5 and the pawn on e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8.}
4. Na4 {[%cal Ga4c5] Goes after the bishop. The knight goes to a4.}
4... Bb6 {Keeps the bishop on the diagonal. Regroups the bishop to b6 and controls d4.}
5. Nxb6 {Wins the bishop pair. Takes the bishop on b6; Black will want to recapture.}
5... axb6 {Black gets the half-open a-file. Recaptures on b6, restoring the material balance.}
6. d4 {[%csl Gd4] Opens lines for the bishops. Claims the centre: the pawn on d4 controls c5 and eyes the pawn on e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1 and the queen on d1.}
)
3. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4f7] Aims at f7. Develops the bishop to c4, where it controls d5.}
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it controls d5 and eyes the pawn on e4.}
4. d3 {[%csl Ge4] Solid: protects e4 and prepares f4. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 supports the bishop on c4 and the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
4... Bc5 {Active development. The bishop on c5 controls d4. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
5. f4 {[%cal Gf4e5] The thematic break, now well prepared. Supports the centre: the pawn on f4 controls g5 and eyes the pawn on e5.}
5... d6 {Holds e5. Supports the centre: the pawn on d6 supports the bishop on c5 and the pawn on e5. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8.}
6. Nf3 {Develops with pressure on e5. The knight on f3 controls d4 and eyes the pawn on e5. That clears the way to castle kingside.} *
